    "roles": ["band_member", "session", "bandleader", "clinician", "author"],
    "summary": "Herbie Hancock's Headhunters drummer from Thrust (1974): Oakland funk played by a jazz drummer. Sixteenths on the hats with the snare and kick talking between them, accents moving through the bar, ghosts leading into them, the hat opened on the off-beats; Actual Proof's intro, every bar different, is the drummers' reference. 'I took parts of Clyde Stubblefield's beat ... and I added a little of my own linear madness.' God Make Me Funky's break (1975), the kick on the sixteenth before 3, became one of hip-hop's most sampled."
  },
